{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l31g34mz","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline","year":2010,"examDate":2010,"subject":"physics","chapter":"waves","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"doppler-effect","type":"integer","marks":3,"negMarks":0,"permalink":"pa-stationary-source-is-emitting-sound-at-a-fixed-frequenc-jee-advanced-physics-waves-6a47gmm1hjismirv","content":"<p>A stationary source is emitting sound at a fixed frequency f<sub>0</sub>, which is reflected by two cars approaching the source. The difference between the frequencies of sound reflected from the cars is 1.2% of f<sub>0</sub>. What is the difference in the speeds of the cars (in km per hour) to the nearest integer? The cars are moving at constant speeds much smaller than the speed of sound which is 330 ms<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>1</sup>.</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"explanation":"<p>Let car B be the observer (moving towards S).</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l31k9j59/94772fbc-256c-4f84-98c9-48fc377749b5/4c6654e0-d126-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31k9j5a.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l31k9j59/94772fbc-256c-4f84-98c9-48fc377749b5/4c6654e0-d126-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31k9j5a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Waves Question 24 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l31k9j59/94772fbc-256c-4f84-98c9-48fc377749b5/4c6654e0-d126-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31k9j5a.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l31k9j59/94772fbc-256c-4f84-98c9-48fc377749b5/4c6654e0-d126-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31k9j5a.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l31k9j59/94772fbc-256c-4f84-98c9-48fc377749b5/4c6654e0-d126-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31k9j5a.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l31k9j59/94772fbc-256c-4f84-98c9-48fc377749b5/4c6654e0-d126-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31k9j5a.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l31k9j59/94772fbc-256c-4f84-98c9-48fc377749b5/4c6654e0-d126-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31k9j5a.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l31k9j59/94772fbc-256c-4f84-98c9-48fc377749b5/4c6654e0-d126-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31k9j5a.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>The frequency observed is</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.798ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"13.368ex\" height=\"2.72ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -849.5 5908.6 1202.3\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D453\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D453\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(523,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1204.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transf